Shortest Path in Undirected graph = Dijkstra's Algorithm 
         HERE use --> queue           HERE --> pq


Algo : 
1. Use a min priority queue to always pick node with smallest distance -> compare with wt/dist
2. For each neighbor, relax edge → update distance if shorter path found
3. Repeat until PQ is empty → final dist[] gives shortest path

Shortest path in DAG :
1. Get topological sort using DFS
2. Initialize distances (∞) and set source node (0) = 0
3. take each node from stack of topo and relax all outgoing edges
4. Update shortest distances and mark unreachable nodes as -1

Bellman ford :
1. Applicable for negative edges/negative cycles too
2. Works only on directed graph
3. If graph is undirected, convert it to directed by directing to both sides

relaxation formula : 
if(dist[u]!=(int)(1e8) && dist[u]+wt < dist[v]){
    dist[v] = dist[u]+wt;
}

Algo :
1. Relax all the edges N-1 times sequentially
2. in last iteration if negative cycle occured return -1 arr
